## §0. METHOD, AND WHAT THIS PASS DELIBERATELY DID NOT REPEAT

The effective text was constructed first: every r-round instruction applied in declared order,
including the two composition orderings r12 declares (§A.3 below). The pass then ran four
routes chosen to be disjoint from the eleven prior passes:

- **(a)** r12's ASSEMBLY against the r1–r11 body — supersession spans, orphan/double-render,
  and the 17-landmark set re-run at r12's own bound.
- **(b)** the THEOREM STATEMENT as effectively amended, read for acceptance, with r12's scope
  clause and its new `d = c_𝒞 v` carrier datum folded.
- **(c)** the FULL S7 consumption sweep at **37** pins (last full run was at 35; the sol r12
  pass ran the dated-append instrument, not the whole quotation/lean sweep).
- **(d)** three new instruments (§D): an exhaustive re-enumeration of every dated append in the
  six sources against r12's eleven-unit record; a **pin-note directive coherence audit**; and a
  master-side closure of the `(OCC)` demand that `(REF-HT)` creates at both levels.

Not repeated (verified by the sol r12 pass, and spot-confirmed only): the byte-minimality of
`HETOW-KEY-BRIDGE-C-A`'s span, the five instance boxes' degree reconciliation, and the
`d = c_𝒞 v` per-instance constants.

