**D.1a — the hardest case, recorded in full because it is the one that could have been a GAP.**
HE6's 2026-08-12 **F-1** (HE6:1061 ff., outside every span) rewrites the γ display *inside*
`HE6-SLOT-SEAM` — the pin the master consumes for `(SLOT-V)` and `(HE6-SEAM)`. It says the
displayed γ "omitted the coefficient normalizers" and directs: read it as
\(\gamma_k(A)=\sum\operatorname{res}(a_{i+e_1t}\pi^{-(k-(i+e_1t)h)/e_1})\eta_\theta^t\) — which is
letter-for-letter the master's `(GAMMA)`, with the corrected conclusion
\(\operatorname{res}(A(\xi)/\varpi(\xi)^k)=\iota_\xi(\gamma_k(A))\eta_\xi^{-q(k)}\) — letter-for-letter
`(HE6-SEAM)`. By r11's own doctrine ("a directive the reader is told to obey is consumed
material") this looks like the r11/r12 shape exactly, and it is dispositioned "touches nothing
this master consumes" at r10 repair 1(g) and again at r11 repair 1(f).

**The disposition holds, and the distinguishing fact is r4 repair 9.** That repair does not read
the corrected formula off HE6-0″'s display; it derives the normalized reading from *another*
pinned span, quoting three grep-verified lines of LEMMA HE3-1L's proof inside `HE3-HE3-1L` that
compute \(c_i\pi^{-(\kappa-(i_0+e_1t)h)/e_1}\) explicitly, and argues that the sources'
"res(c_i)" abbreviates the height-normalized coefficient — an argument the source's own A3
verification independently reproduces ("the tying coefficients have positive valuation
\((k-jh)/e_1\), so the bare res(a_j) reading is vacuous"). So the master's consumption has a
pinned supplier that does not route through the dated correction, and obeying the correction
changes nothing it reads. Contrast the β-guard, which r11 *did* pin: there no alternative pinned
leg supplied well-posedness. **The two dispositions are consistent; no finding.** (One residue is
recorded as a nit at §F.3.)

