### D.3 Instrument 3 — closing the `(OCC)` demand that `(REF-HT)` creates, master-side

r6 repair 1(a) records that after `(REF-HT)`, "`(OCC)` is now read at a determined height: the
visible domain obligation for this transition is \(\lambda\in H_{\mathrm{lift}}(B)\)". The note
leaves the fullness of \(\lambda\) to the carrier and cites HE7:925's parenthetical
("it exists: λ₂ > T₂ satisfies (‡₂) by §S4.3") as corroboration. No pass has checked that the
master's own displayed sufficient bounds actually cover the refinement height. They do, at both
levels:

- **Level one.** Full ⟸ \(k\ge(D'-1)h\) (S1.4's uniform sufficient bound). Every side slope has
  \(\lambda>T=D'h>(D'-1)h\). ✓
- **Level two.** `(FULL2-U)`: \(k\ge(\ell d_r-1)u+\ell(D'-1)h\). With \(T_2=\ell d_r u\),
  \[
  T_2-\bigl[(\ell d_r-1)u+\ell(D'-1)h\bigr]=u-\ell(D'-1)h>0
  \]
  because \(u=\ell\lambda>\ell D'h\). Hence \(T_2\) already exceeds the bound, so every level-two
  side slope \(\lambda_2>T_2\) (clause 1) satisfies `(FULL2-U)` and is full. ✓

So the `(OCC)` demand at the product-1 transition is discharged from the master's own displays at
both levels, and HE7:925's parenthetical is genuinely corroboration rather than the only leg.
**Recorded as a strengthening available to the note; no finding.**

