## §E. FINDINGS

### E.1 m-1 (MINOR, on r12's own text) — r12 repair 1(g)'s ground for the HE7:2478 disposition is false as written

**The text.** r12 repair 1(g), the dated-append sweep over the five non-HE6 sources, master
line 4333:

> - HE7:2478 (post-annex-acceptance, riders M-1, M-A, M-B): M-1 is a run-record counter and M-A
>   an oracle name, neither consumed; M-B is a provenance rider on THEOREM HE7.D's §S2 clause and
>   COROLLARY HE7.B(ii), **and this master names neither.**

**Why it is false.** The master names both, verbatim, at line 2136 (r3 repair 1(b)):

> The chain's actual endpoint units, named verbatim: **ANNEX-DEF HE7-2′** (the corrected level
> recursion) and **ANNEX-COROLLARY R1-d** (THEOREM HE7.D and COROLLARY HE7.B(ii), re-proved).

`grep -n 'HE7\.D\|HE7\.B'` over the master returns exactly two lines: 2136 and 4333 itself.
The sentence is wrong in the note's **own vocabulary**: the standing S7 check r4 repair 13
installed is worded "every source display the master text **quotes, names, or leans on**", so
"names" is a relation the gate tracks, and the master bears it to both units at 2136.

**Why the disposition nevertheless stands** (so this is a minor and not a gap): the operative
test is consumption, as r12's own restated S5 item 3 says in terms ("Consumption, not citation,
is the gated relation"). The 2136 naming is a unit-identification parenthetical describing what
the pinned endpoint `ANNEX-COROLLARY R1-d` re-proves — it is drawn from HE7's own R1 heading
(HE7:1990) and leans on neither THEOREM HE7.D's §S2 clause nor COROLLARY HE7.B(ii)'s
inductive-step clause. Obeying M-B (read those two clauses with (SLOT) := ANNEX-THEOREM R1-b,
(LIFT) := ANNEX-THEOREM R1-c, §S5 transfer audited per R1.2) changes nothing the master reads:
the master reads the cocycle chain for `(COC-DEF)`/`(BETA)`, and R1-b, R1-c and R1-d all lie
inside `HE7-COCYCLE-2P-THROUGH-R1D` [2013, 2253]. So M-B is not consumed — on the consumption
ground, not on the naming ground.

**Classification: MINOR**, of the bookkeeping-on-r12's-own-text kind. It is one sentence in this
round's own new sweep record; nothing depends on it; the cure is to replace the false ground with
the true one and to classify the 2136 naming under the unit-identification/boundary-fixing class
that r12 repair 3 has just created. No display, hypothesis, pin, fence or obligation moves.

